## 🔧 Plug it into your agent

**[Connection table](configs/README.md)** — base URLs, keys and client notes for {{ endpoint_count }} live OpenAI-compatible APIs, plus available Claude Code routes and direct Codex profiles. [Copy buttons on the website]({{ pages_url }}/#connections). These configs are regenerated on every update:

- [`configs/opencode.json`](configs/opencode.json) — [opencode](https://opencode.ai) providers: keys via `{env:...}`, keyless endpoints ready to use
- [`configs/litellm.yaml`](configs/litellm.yaml) — [LiteLLM](https://docs.litellm.ai): `{{ litellm_command }}` serves the listed models locally{% if litellm_groups %}; {{ litellm_groups | either_code }} falls back between free lanes{% endif %}. Set each lane's own key: otherwise LiteLLM forwards `OPENAI_API_KEY`{{ '' }}
- [`configs/claude-code.sh`](configs/claude-code.sh) — `source` it for [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs) functions with the listed keys and models
- [`{{ codex.path }}`]({{ codex.path }}) — Copy to `~/.codex/`; run `codex -p {{ codex.name }}`. [Codex CLI](https://developers.openai.com/codex) uses Responses; LiteLLM translates to chat completions (Codex CLI {{ codex.since }}, LiteLLM {{ codex.litellm_since }} or later)
- [`configs/free-llm.env.example`](configs/free-llm.env.example) — Commented env exports for any OpenAI-compatible tool
- [`llms.txt`](llms.txt){{ dot }}[`index.json`](index.json){{ dot }}[feed]({{ feed_url }}) — Text for agents, the JSON registry and the Atom changelog
- [`browse.html`]({{ pages_url }}/browse.html){{ dot }}[provider pages]({{ pages_url }}/providers/) — Filterable list, full offers, connections, evidence and history

## 📡 How this list stays fresh

Discovery, verification and publication:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    S["🌐 web scout<br/>Tavily · HN · GitHub · feeds · models.dev"] --> L["🧠 LLM extract<br/>(evidence only)"]
    L --> G{"🛡 probe gate"}
    G -->|verified| PR["📬 pull request"]
    PR -->|human merge| R[("registry.yaml")]
    R --> P{"📡 live probes<br/>{{ schedule }}"}
    P -->|pass| V["✅ verified date updated"]
    P -->|fail ×{{ archive_after_failures }} · stale {{ archive_after_days }}d · shutdown announced| A["📦 Archive"]
    R -->|render| MD["README.md<br/>(this page)"]

    classDef pass fill:#3fb95022,stroke:#3fb950,stroke-width:2px
    classDef drop fill:#f8514922,stroke:#f85149,stroke-width:2px
    classDef human fill:#58a6ff22,stroke:#58a6ff,stroke-width:2px
    classDef store fill:#8957e522,stroke:#8957e5,stroke-width:2px
    class G,P,V pass
    class A drop
    class PR,MD human
    class R store
```

- **Live probes, {{ schedule }}.** A passing GitHub Actions probe earns the verified date. Model IDs, quotas, prices or vendor sentences anchor the offer; the word "free" alone does not. Keyless lanes receive real keyless requests. Bot walls mean "could not check", not "gone".
- **Probe-gated discovery.** Tavily, Hacker News, GitHub, curated feeds and zero-cost models.dev providers supply fetched evidence for LLM extraction. Candidates need a passing live probe and a reviewed pull request; the LLM writes neither this README nor `main`.
- **Self-pruning, never silent.** {{ archive_after_failures }} consecutive failed probes, {{ archive_after_days }} days without a pass, an announced shutdown or a reviewer's delisting move a row to the [Archive](#-archive) with its reason. Rows are never deleted. Arrivals, departures and free-model changes remain in [`history.jsonl`](history.jsonl) and the [Atom feed]({{ feed_url }}).

Sources, expiry rules and contribution requirements are in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).

